<title>USA: Xircom to sell 12.5 pct to Intel.</title>
<headline>Xircom to sell 12.5 pct to Intel.</headline>
<dateline>THOUSAND OAKS, Calif 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Xircom Inc said on Thursday it had signed an agreement with Intel Corp, the world's largest chip maker, in which Intel will purchase a 12.5 percent interest of the company's stock (2.5 million newly issued shares) and acquire warrants to obtain an additional 7.5 percent of the company's stock (1.5 million shares).</p>
<p>The value of the initial Intel equity investment in Xircom is $52 million, Xircom said.</p>
<p>In addition, Xircom said it and Intel have signed a three-year technology and multi-million dollar OEM agreement.</p>
</text>
